In article <7827@stewart> bruce@Software.Mitel.COM (Bruce Clement) writes:

>I think perhaps only wizards, priests, elves and tourists should be able to
>choose.

A humble question: why? 

>How about making the healing spell sensitive to alignment and ask you for a
>direction when you cast it.  If you are standing by a lawfull monster and
>you are chaotic you could cast the heal spell at the monster and do damage
>because of opposite alignments.

Am I the only one here to whom this sounds very silly? Alignment is a general
rule for players/monsters to live by. Other than that nothing else should have
an alignment. This includes objects, spells, magic, but not items that have
their own will (of which there are currently _none_ in nethack.) An example
would be an intelligent lawful sword (you make a fancy name for it!) Such
a sword could decide to attack non-friendly monsters. An intelligent chaotic
sword could decide to attack just anybody, including the wielder!

ANOTHER TOPIC that just came to my mind from this: you (me! see the list
of depraved individuals :-) are developing nethack, but where to? If you are
a bus driver and just start driving you are bound get somewhere, but I bet
it is not where you wanted to go!

I can see where the current road is going: into AD&D land. Forget it! Nethack
cannot compete with AD&D (tm) on its own ground. For one thing, we cannot
supply the player with thick volumes full of complicated rules. And there is
no intelligent DM in nethack (computers are stupid.) Nethack was once very
different from (A)D&D and I think it was better but that is just a personal
opinion. If I were to play nethack again (beat nethack 1.x and 3.x), I would
probably get a copy of an old version..
